-- title:
--   Base change of the pole chart of the two-chart integral model
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $F$ a field that is an $R$-algebra, $j \in F$ with $j \neq 0$, and $O$ a commutative $R$-algebra. Write $B =$ `chartAlgInf R F j` for the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of the elements of $F$ integral over the $R$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$, let $X$ be the two-chart integral model, i.e. the pushout of the two morphisms `fFin R F j` and `fInf R F j`, with structure morphism `toBase R F j : X ⟶ Spec R` obtained by descending the two structure morphisms of the charts, and let `ιInf R F j` be the pole-chart morphism $\operatorname{Spec} B \to X$. The assertion is that there exists a morphism $g : \operatorname{Spec}(B \otimes_R O) \to X \times_{\operatorname{Spec} R} \operatorname{Spec} O$, the pullback being taken along `Spec.map` of the structure map $R \to O$, such that: $g$ is an open immersion; $g$ followed by the first projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $b \mapsto b \otimes 1$ followed by `ιInf R F j`; $g$ followed by the second projection equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $o \mapsto 1 \otimes o$; and the range of $g$ on underlying topological spaces is exactly the preimage, under the first projection, of the open image of the whole of $\operatorname{Spec} B$ under `ιInf R F j`.
--
--   This identifies the pole chart of the base change of the two-chart integral model to $O$ with the affine scheme $\operatorname{Spec}(B \otimes_R O)$, compatibly with both projections, so that points of the base-changed model lying over the pole chart and their local rings may be read off from $B \otimes_R O$. It is the pole-chart counterpart of the corresponding statement for the finite chart, and is used in the verification that fibres of the full-level modular curve model are regular at points of the pole chart.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel_exists_isOpenImmersion_spec_tensor_chartAlgInf.lean

